-- title:
--   Quotient-graph presentation of the Mumford side at q'
-- statement:
--   The data are as follows. Rational numbers $a_2,b_2$ and natural numbers $N,q,q'$ with $N$ nonzero, $N$ squarefree ($hN$), $q$ and $q'$ prime, $q\nmid N$ ($hqN$), $q'\nmid N$ ($hq'N$), $q'\ne q$ ($hqq'$) and $5\le q$, $5\le q'$ ($hq5$, $hq'5$).
--
--   Quaternionic level data: $hdef_2$ says that $a_2<0$, $b_2<0$, and that a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ has $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ a division algebra exactly when $q$ lies in $v$; $\Lambda_2,R_2$ are $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]$ with $\Lambda_2$ a maximal order ($h\Lambda_2$), $R_2$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ in the first ($hR_2$), and $R_2\le\Lambda_2$ ($hR\Lambda_2$). A finite idele $n_2$ lies in `primeHeckeSet R₂ q'` ($hn_2$), the set of units whose image lies in the finite adelic box of $R_2$ and whose inverse lies there after scaling by $q'$ but not unscaled, and whose $q'^{-1}$-multiple is not in the box. Further: `meetOrder R₂ n₂` $=R_2\cap R_2^{n_2}$ is Eichler of level $Nq'$ ($hS_2$), is stable under conjugation by $n_2$ ($hnorm_2$), the shift by $n_2$ on the class set of the finite-idele stabiliser of `meetOrder R₂ n₂` is an involution ($hsq_2$), the class sets of the stabilisers of `meetOrder R₂ n₂` and of $R_2$ are finite, and $hlaws_2$ is `ClassSetHeckeLaws N q' Λ₂ R₂ n₂`: the edge Hecke matrices commute pairwise, the vertex Hecke matrices commute pairwise, for $\ell\ne q'$ the edge operators are equivariant for both degeneracy maps of `classSetDegeneracyData R₂ n₂`, and the joint kernel of those maps is stable under every edge operator.
--
--   Place and tower data: a valuation subring $A_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q'$ a nonunit of $A_1$ ($hA_1$); a field $FN$, a curve over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and essentially of finite type over it; a tower $\mathbb T$ of Hecke data of type $(q,q')$ over $FN$, whose index objects are $\mathrm{Obj}=\mathrm{Option}\{\ell\text{ prime},\ \ell\ne q,q'\}$ and whose arrows are pairs $(\ell,i)$ with $i\in\{0,1\}$, each arrow going from $\mathrm{some}\ \ell$ to $\mathrm{none}$; $hfg$ asserts that each field $\mathbb T.\mathrm{objField}\ j$ contains a transcendental element over which it is finite. Galois and Atkin–Lehner semilinear data: homomorphisms $galN$, $galT_\ell$ from the decomposition subgroup of $A_1$ over $\mathbb Q$ to the semilinear automorphism groups of $FN$ and of $\mathbb T.F\ \ell$, whose base parts are the given field automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ ($hgalN$, $hgalT$), together with families $W$, $WT$ of semilinear automorphisms indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\ 2$. The decomposition subgroup acts isometrically for the valuation of $A_1$ ($hiso_1$), and $v_1$ is a finite place of $\mathbb Q$ containing $q'$ ($hv_1$).
--
--   Čerednik–Drinfeld parameters: an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_1$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]$ into $2\times2$ matrices over $K_0:=$ [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₁`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13) (the closure of the prime subfield inside the completion of $A_1$ at its valuation), and $\rho_1:\mathbb H^\times\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ given by projectivising $\iota_1$ ($h\rho_1$); a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi_1$ of $K_0$ inside the completion whose image is $q'$ ($h\varpi_1$), with the holomorphic ring `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ₁ ρ₁` a domain. Elements $s_1(\ell)\in\mathbb H^\times$ and finite ideles $sf_1(\ell)$ satisfy $hs_1$: $sf_1(\ell)$ is the diagonal image of $s_1(\ell)$ at all places not containing $q'$, is $1$ at places containing $q'$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_1(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₂ (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` if $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_1(\ell))=\ell$.
--
--   Level groups and involutions: subgroups $\Gamma_1(j)\le\mathbb H^\times$ with $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})$ consisting of the units lying in `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₂ v₁` (units that are locally in the group generated by the local unit box of $R_2$ at every place other than $v_1$) whose reduced norm has even $q'$-valuation ($h\Gamma_10$), and $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{some}\ \ell)=\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})\cap s_1(\ell)\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})s_1(\ell)^{-1}$ ($h\Gamma_1\ell$). Units $w_1(j),\bar w_1(j)$ satisfy: $hw_1$, that $w_1(\mathrm{none})$ lies in `awayUnits R₂ v₁` and $w_1(\mathrm{some}\ \ell)$ in `awayUnits (meetOrder R₂ (sf₁ ℓ)) v₁`, each of reduced norm $q'$; and $hwbar_1$, that each $\bar w_1(j)$ has reduced norm $q$, is a local unit of the relevant order at all places $u\ne v_1$ not containing $q$, and conjugation by it preserves both the local box of that order and the local box of $\Lambda_2$ at every $u\ne v_1$.
--
--   Analytic descent data: $dIso_1$ sends the decomposition group into the isometric automorphisms of the completion, realising the Galois action ($hdIso_1$); $\chi_1$ is a quadratic character of the decomposition group; $\iota^M_1(j)$ embeds $\mathbb T.\mathrm{objField}\ j$ into $\mathrm{Frac}$ of the holomorphic ring; and $hI$ asserts `DescentIntertwining q' 1 0 A₁ ρ₁ ϖ₁ Γ₁ w₁ wbar₁ s₁ dIso₁ FN 𝕋 galN galT W WT χ₁ ιM₁`, the predicate tying the character $\chi_1$ to inertia and Frobenius at $q'$ and the embeddings $\iota^M_1$ to the Galois and Atkin–Lehner data of the tower, with the two distinguished indices taken to be $1$ and $0$.
--
--   Residue and symmetry data: $R_0$ is a discrete valuation domain with finite residue field, an $R_0$-algebra structure on $K_0$ making $K_0$ its fraction field, whose image is exactly the set of elements of valuation at most $1$ in the completion ($hR_0$). $S_1$ is a group with homomorphisms $scalar_1:S_1\to D$ and $\iota S_1:D\to S_1$ splitting it ($h\iota S_1$), where $D$ is the decomposition subgroup; distinguished elements $\sigma_{01},\sigma_{11}$; characters $\chi S_1:S_1\to\mathbb Z/2$ and $sgn_1:S_1\to\mathbb Z^\times$; and semilinear actions $galFC_1(j)$ of $S_1$ on the invariant field $\mathfrak M(\Gamma_1 j)$ of $\Gamma_1(j)$ inside $\mathrm{Frac}$ of the holomorphic ring. These satisfy: $hgen_1$, every element of $S_1$ is $\iota S_1(\tau)\sigma_{01}^u\sigma_{11}^v$; $hrel_1$, the two elements are commuting involutions, each central for the image of $\iota S_1$; $huniv_1$, the corresponding universal property of $S_1$ among groups with such data; $h\chi S_1$, that $\chi S_1\circ\iota S_1=\chi_1$, $\chi S_1(\sigma_{01})\ne1$ and $\chi S_1(\sigma_{11})=1$; $hsgnS_1$, that $sgn_1\circ\iota S_1$ is $1$ where $\chi S_1$ is trivial and equals $sgn_1(\sigma_{01})$ elsewhere, with $sgn_1(\sigma_{01})=-1$ and $sgn_1(\sigma_{11})=1$; $hbase_1$, that the base automorphism of $galFC_1(j)(\sigma)$ is $dIso_1(scalar_1\sigma)$; and the action formulae $hactD_1$ ($\iota S_1(\tau)$ acts by the coefficient automorphism induced by $dIso_1(\tau)$ followed by multiplication by $1$ or $w_1(j)$ according as $\chi_1(\tau)$ is trivial or not), $hact_{01}$ ($\sigma_{01}$ acts by $w_1(j)$) and $hact_{11}$ ($\sigma_{11}$ acts by $\bar w_1(j)$).
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist: finite types $E_j,V_j$ with decidable equality, for each $j\in\mathrm{Obj}(q,q')$ a degeneracy datum $D_j$ on $(E_j,V_j)$ (two maps $a,b:E_j\to V_j$ and a width $w:E_j\to\mathbb N_{>0}$); bijections $eV_j$ from the orbit set of $\rho_1(\Gamma_1 j)$ on the vertices [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex R₀ K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) to $V_j$, and $eE_j$ from the set of orbits of darts of the Bruhat–Tits tree `BruhatTits.tree R₀ K₀` whose chosen representative has origin of type $0$ relative to the standard vertex to $E_j$; homomorphisms $\pi V_1(j),\pi E_1(j)$ of $S_1$ into the permutation groups of $V_j$ and $E_j$; a homomorphism $actZ_1(j)$ of $S_1$ into the $\mathbb Z$-linear automorphisms of the ribbon kernel of $D_j$ (the intersection of the kernels of the two pushforwards along $a$ and $b$); a bijection $cE_1$ from the class set of the finite-idele stabiliser of `meetOrder R₂ n₂` to $E_{\mathrm{none}}$; a $\mathbb Z$-linear isomorphism $e_1$ from the ribbon kernel of $D_{\mathrm{none}}$ to that of `classSetDegeneracyData R₂ n₂`; and for every arrow $\alpha$ a finite homomorphism $\mu F_1(\alpha)$ of degeneracy data from $D_{\mathrm{dom}\,\alpha}$ to $D_{\mathrm{cod}\,\alpha}$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   Geometric presentation. For every $j$ the image $\rho_1(\Gamma_1 j)$ is type-preserving for the tree with base the standard vertex, and every dart has finite stabiliser in $\rho_1(\Gamma_1 j)$. Through $eE_j$ and $eV_j$ the map $a$ of $D_j$ is the orbit of the origin of the representative dart, the map $b$ is the orbit of its terminus, and the width $w$ is the cardinality of the stabiliser of that dart in $\rho_1(\Gamma_1 j)$.
--
--   Transport of semilinear symmetries. For every $j$, every $\sigma\in S_1$, every $n$ in the normaliser of $\Gamma_1(j)$ in $\mathbb H^\times$ and every isometric automorphism $t$ of the completion: if $\sigma$ acts on $\mathfrak M(\Gamma_1 j)$ by multiplication by $n$ composed with the coefficient automorphism induced by $t$, then $\pi V_1(j)(\sigma)$ is the permutation of $V_j$ induced by $v\mapsto\rho_1(n)\cdot v$, and for every edge $e$: if $\rho_1(n)$ is type-preserving then $sgn_1(\sigma)=1$ and $\pi E_1(j)(\sigma)$ sends $e$ to the orbit of $\rho_1(n)\cdot e$, while if $\rho_1(n)$ is not type-preserving then $sgn_1(\sigma)=-1$ and $\pi E_1(j)(\sigma)$ sends $e$ to the orbit of the reversed dart $(\rho_1(n)\cdot e)^{\mathrm{symm}}$.
--
--   Inertia behaviour and compatibilities. For every $j$ and $\tau$ in the decomposition group: if $\chi S_1(\iota S_1\tau)=1$ then $\pi V_1(j)(\iota S_1\tau)$ and $\pi E_1(j)(\iota S_1\tau)$ are the identity and $sgn_1(\iota S_1\tau)=1$; if $\chi S_1(\iota S_1\tau)\ne1$ then these permutations agree with those of $\sigma_{01}$ and $sgn_1(\iota S_1\tau)=sgn_1(\sigma_{01})$. The action of $S_1$ preserves the widths; elements of sign $+1$ commute with $a$ and with $b$, while elements of sign $-1$ interchange them; and $actZ_1(j)(\sigma)$ acts on functions in the ribbon kernel by $(actZ_1(j)(\sigma)x)(\pi E_1(j)(\sigma)e')=sgn_1(\sigma)\,x(e')$.
--
--   Identification at level $N$. Under $cE_1$ the permutation $\pi E_1(\mathrm{none})(\sigma_{01})$ is the shift by $n_2$ on the class set; $e_1$ is the map on ribbon kernels induced by $cE_1$ coordinatewise; $e_1$ preserves the ribbon Gram pairing, that is $\mathrm{ribbonGram}(\mathrm{classSetDegeneracyData}\ R_2\ n_2)(e_1x,e_1y)=\mathrm{ribbonGram}(D_{\mathrm{none}})(x,y)$; and conjugating $actZ_1(\mathrm{none})(\sigma_{11})$ by $e_1$ gives the Hecke kernel map at the prime $q$ of `classSetHeckeData N q' Λ₂ R₂ n₂`.
--
--   Hecke transport along the arrows. For every arrow $\alpha=(\ell,i)$, write $g_\alpha=\rho_1(1)$ if $i=0$ and $g_\alpha=\rho_1(s_1(\ell))$ if $i=1$. Then $\mu F_1(\alpha)$ acts on vertices by $v\mapsto g_\alpha^{-1}\cdot v$ and on edges by $e\mapsto g_\alpha^{-1}\cdot e$, read through $eV$ and $eE$ at source and target; its total degree equals `HeckeTower.arrowDegree N α`, namely $\ell$ if $\ell\mid N$ and $\ell+1$ otherwise; its edge map commutes with the $S_1$-actions $\pi E_1$; and for every away prime $\ell$, transporting by $e_1$ the composite of pullback along $\mu F_1(\ell,1)$ followed by pushforward along $\mu F_1(\ell,0)$ gives the Hecke kernel map at $\ell$ of `classSetHeckeData N q' Λ₂ R₂ n₂`.
--
--   This is the Mumford-side (Čerednik–Drinfeld) input at the auxiliary prime $q'$: the quotient of the Bruhat–Tits tree by the $q'$-adic level groups coming from a definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q$ is presented as a finite degeneracy datum, with the action of the decomposition group together with the two Atkin–Lehner involutions, the identification of the level-$N$ edge set with a quaternionic class set, and the Hecke correspondences realised as push–pull along the tower arrows. It feeds the construction of a Shimura-curve model with good reduction and an equivariant uniformisation at the two places.
